According to the Book, a type-3 fu'ivla can be made with a rafsi of form CC=
V,=20
CVC, CVCC, or CCVC. AFAIK, some of us (including me) consider fu'ivla of th=
e=20
form CCVrCV... or CCVnrV... to be of type 4. Looking through jbovlaste, I=
=20
found one of that form: "plargoni", which means not some kind of planner bu=
t=20
a geranium. There's another one, "turdunu" (bullroarer, from some Aborigina=
l=20
language), which I made up originally as "turndunu" but changed=20
because "turndunu" is a type-3. jbofi'e considers "plargoni" to be of type =
4.=20
Should CCV rafsi be disallowed in type-3 fu'ivla?

Also, it should be stated clearly that if a type-3 fu'ivla can be interpret=
ed=20
as starting with a CVC or CVCC rafsi, it is interpreted as starting with a=
=20
CVCC rafsi. Otherwise some combinations of gismu and foreign part cannot be=
=20
turned into a type-3 fu'ivla.

Pierre
